{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes","id":1448437,"title":"Renaming the Indigenous Tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-13T10:52:41-07:00","id":1448437,"title":"Renaming the Indigenous Tribes","content":"<span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So for the unaware, the name of &quot;Older Brother&quot; and &quot;Younger Brother&quot; in Werewolf the Apocalypse, are... not terms that were appropriate for largely white writers to do what they wanted with, and not really appropriate for the game table. So I'm looking to tweak the setting a bit at my table to be more respectful to Native concerns, while keeping what is cool about the two Garou tribes in question.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">For Older Brother, my best idea so far is &quot;Whisper Keepers&quot;, but I'm told the end sound repetition doesn't make it sound great. So I'm open to other suggestions. Their Tribal Spirit* is Horned Serpent (a broad archetype that includes their original namesake, but also less &quot;sacred secret&quot; figures).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">For Younger Brother, the leading contender currently is &quot;Winter Claws&quot;. Their Tribal Spirit* is Great Fisher (Kitchi-Odjig).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In addition to this, there are Greed Banes that possess humans who commit cannibalism, and create fomori called Ice Hearts - these have another in setting name, but not one that I'd use at the game table. The Winter Claws (or whatever Younger Brother ends up being named) have a particular hate for these monsters. Peter Culliford, of the Pentex Board, may be one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">*Totem is a grossly misused term that does not mean what white writers keep using it to mean. The Background is instead just called &quot;Pack Spirit&quot;, and the Tribe Patrons are &quot;Tribal Spirits&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Does anyone have any alternate suggestions for evocative names for these two Tribes that respect Native prohibitions on the usage of certain concepts and terms?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T10:57:51-07:00","id":1448439,"title":"","content":"If the name hadn't already been used, I'd suggest White Howlers for the Wendigo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T11:02:56-07:00","id":1448440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448439#post1448439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the name hadn't already been used, I'd suggest White Howlers for the Wendigo.</div> </div> </div> </div>honestly the thought of going \u201chow many tribes based on Northern European early medieval Sagas do we need?\u201d and throwing the Fianna and the Get together as the White Howlers (with some more culturally specific camps) has crossed my mind. But I\u2019d need to come up with a new origin for the Spiral Dancers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T15:07:24-07:00","id":1448472,"title":"","content":"Something that I struggle with when considering such things (beyond being a white person who doesn't have any say in what's ultimately appropriate for someone else's cultural representation in the game): do you want to keep a sense of cultural distinction with the American First Peoples based Tribes?<br /> <br /> &quot;Winter Claws&quot; certainly works better than Wendigo on a number of levels. But since it puts them in line with the other Garou Tribes in how their name is constructed, they lose a bit of distinctiveness that you'd assume Two(/Three, Middle Brother needs a better name too if even less relevant to playing in the modern day) Tribes separated from the rest of the Garou Nation for thousands of years would develop. Though that goes the other way in considering how the Children of Gaia, Get of Fenris, and Fianna all buck the normal Tribal naming pattern and maybe need to be adjusted as well (combining the Fianna and Fenrir or not) if you want to consider having a subtle but distinctive difference.<br /> <br /> I think it would be good if, when looking at the list of Tribes, you can tell that something is different about Older and Younger Brother, without it being as on the nose as it currently is. If the Eurasian Tribes developed a two-word pattern, and the American Tribes a three-word pattern, it could be a nice way to maintain that sense of lingering cultural divide without leaning into anything inherently appropriative; though the BSDs might need a rename as well so you don't create a problem there, but I think the number of words isn't the only thing that matters is the types of words are juggle properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T17:23:00-07:00","id":1448479,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I suppose in a prefect hindsight version of Werewolf, the three North American tribes would be the White Howlers, the Earth Walkers, and the Hunters in Darkness, with the Celtic tribe being the Fire Touched, the Germanic one being the Red Talons, and the all-wolf one being the Predator Kings maybe. (The Bunyip would probably be a Changing Breed instead of a tribe.)<br /> <br /> Maybe Wind Howlers and Secret Seekers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T17:57:54-07:00","id":1448483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448479#post1448479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe Wind Howlers and Secret Seekers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m leaning toward Dusk Keepers right now, but something Wind did cross my mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T18:19:55-07:00","id":1448485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448479#post1448479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I suppose in a prefect hindsight version of Werewolf, the three North American tribes would be the White Howlers, the Earth Walkers, and the Hunters in Darkness, with the Celtic tribe being the Fire Touched, the Germanic one being the Red Talons, and the all-wolf one being the Predator Kings maybe. (The Bunyip would probably be a Changing Breed instead of a tribe.)<br /> <br /> Maybe Wind Howlers and Secret Seekers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In an ideal Hindsight version the Game would have been Called WereBeast and had the various Fera get much more central focus from the start, with probably fewer Garou tribes to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T18:26:44-07:00","id":1448487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazyjabberwock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448485#post1448485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In an ideal Hindsight version the Game would have been Called WereBeast and had the various Fera get much more central focus from the start, with probably fewer Garou tribes to start with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, werewolves were the most well known of such things, especially in North America in the early 90s. But if you were going to go with that route, I'd have probably suggested about 7 werewolf tribes, and then added to that ones from real world lore - leopards, hyena, sharks, jaguars, and tigers; maybe also foxes - in the Players Guide. Not sure what I'd call them all though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T18:46:43-07:00","id":1448488,"title":"","content":"naturally werewolves have ubiquity for good reason, and the war of rage makes a very good bit of past baggage for everyone involved for drama.<br /> <br /> as for the Three Brothers, I kinda find myself stumped and just roll with it as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T23:29:56-07:00","id":1448489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448479#post1448479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (The Bunyip would probably be a Changing Breed instead of a tribe.)</div> </div> </div> </div>And they wouldn't be called Bunyip.<br /> <br /> Actually they probably shouldn't exist at all. Thylacines are basically absent from traditional Dreaming stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T10:10:08-07:00","id":1448521,"title":"","content":"I personally use Older Brother, Middle Brother, and Younger Brother but I can understand why those wouldn\u2019t be particularly attractive as primary names.<br /> <br /> For Older Brother I\u2019ve heard of \u2018Bane Tenders\u2019 and I can also imagine names like \u2018Dark Whisperers\u2019, \u2018Shadow Wresters\u2019, or \u2018Serpent Handlers\u2019. I can also see \u2018Whisper Keepers\u2019 and I also tend to handle their tribal patron as \u201cHorned Serpent\u201d with a focus on the dangerous but rewarding task of delving underground or into dark/secret places to discover hidden/powerful knowledge. <br /> <br /> For Middle Brother I\u2019ve heard \u2018Land Keepers\u2019 or \u2018Earth Walkers\u2019, \u2018World Speakers\u2019, or \u2018Law Tellers\u2019. For their tribal patron I usually keep it as something like Turtle or \u201cLand Turtle\u201d with an emphasis on the steady and enduring laws and orders of the world kept by tradition and communion with your environment, history, and society.<br /> <br /> For Younger Brother I\u2019ve heard \u2018Ice Hearts\u2019 and I can imagine options like \u2018Ice Hunters\u2019, \u2018Wind Biters\u2019, and I can certainly see \u2018Winter Claws\u2019. For their tribal patron I usually use something like \u201cForest Man/Hairy Man\u201d, somewhat inspired by the already apparent use of Sasquatch but also references I\u2019ve found in other indigenous American cultures in my research and seemed to have both a primeval wilderness and custom keeper elements. I can also see how Great Fisher would work well though.<br /> <br /> For the Australian \u201cGarou\u201d I usually have them be a unique fera native to Australia that was post-humously inducted into the nation by guilty and grieving garou. I usually call them something like the \u2018Song Keepers\u2019 and place a focus on their being keepers of rituals and oral histories, now lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T11:24:36-07:00","id":1448525,"title":"","content":"While I'm not sure we need a 14th Tribe, it seems like it would be easier to take the singing dogs and dingoes and have them be one larger Tribe. Dingoes actually do have a long standing place in Aboriginal culture, and whether or not you want to have any marsupial Fera (in the past or in the present) can be a different issue from the Garou specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T12:04:35-07:00","id":1448528,"title":"","content":"Yeah why where their two werewolf tribes in a relatively small part of Europe? But like two in all of Asia and 3 in the Americas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T13:57:03-07:00","id":1448534,"title":"","content":"I think the Asian Garou thing can be improved by placing more significance on the presence that did arrive there and leaning on the metaplot angle that the Fera were more victorious in the Wars of Rage in tar region so there\u2019s less of a Garou hegemony (perhaps even you could say that a local garou tribe was destroyed during the Wars of Rage).<br /> <br /> I think with general tribes like the Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Red Talons having been around for a very long time helps with that; plus you have the Stargazers around the Himalayas and the Children of Gaia in India. I also think having waves of Shadow Lord &amp; Silver Fangs in East Asia, as is already somewhat indicated with the Hakken, can be done to fill things out and maybe even homebrew a Silver Fang house or two or say some of the lost houses survived in Asia. I also have a homebrewed camp/micro-tribe that I use to populate Central Asia and Mongolia but I agree that none of this extra effort would be necessary if White Wolf hadn\u2019t made Asia so distinct as a setting to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T15:10:08-07:00","id":1448540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448528#post1448528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah why where their two werewolf tribes in a relatively small part of Europe? But like two in all of Asia and 3 in the Americas</div> </div> </div> </div>The history of the setting makes this... not as bad as it could be. The real big outliers are the White Howlers.<br /> <br /> The Fianna's pre-Phoenician expansion territory included modern day: Portugal, Spain, France, and the UK, with the Get of Fenris controlling Norway, Sweden, Finland, Denmark, Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania, and Poland. That's not exactly small parts of Europe. With the Black Furies making up most of southern Europe, and the Shadow Lords expanding into the area from the Caucus range.<br /> <br /> So the White Howlers only being from a part of the UK? That's definitely the oddball.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs both traditionally claimed territories on the Europe/Asia border. The Silver Fangs have three Houses that are mostly Asian (Crescent Moon over northern Asia, Wise Heart over western Asia, and Blood Red Crest over the Indian sub-continent). The Children of Gaia explicitly started in the Fertile Crescent, while the Shadow Lords and Glass Walkers have later, but significant numbers in the Middle Kingdom (the fact that the Middle Kingdom is its own separate thing is a huge portion of the problem here). And of course the Stargazers.<br /> <br /> South America also runs into the problem that sub-Saharan Africa does: a lack of significant populations of wolves to drawn on for cultural inspirations for Tribes from there, and the game being weird about canids that count or don't for these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448534#post1448534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">plus you have the Stargazers around the Himalayas...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, you can fix a lot by expanding the Stargazers so they're not a tiny group of Buddhist monks that refuse to reproduce with the large wolf and human populations around them. As I've gone on about in other threads, the Stargazers could easily be one of the largest Tribes, and add a lot more to Asian representation in the Garou nation; esp, if you have an Asian/Oceania Tribe made of expanding out the singing dogs/dingoes into something more.<br /> <br /> Though we're getting away from brain-storming names for the American Tribes.<br /> <br /> I'm still curious if other people have thoughts about my idea of using more neutral names, but ones that still denote a difference in culture. While it might have been facetious, if the American Tribes had names in the format like Hunters in Darkness, instead of Shadow Lords is an example of a way you can do something to address what I did before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T16:26:21-07:00","id":1448546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448525#post1448525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm not sure we need a 14th Tribe, it seems like it would be easier to take the singing dogs and dingoes and have them be one larger Tribe. Dingoes actually do have a long standing place in Aboriginal culture, and whether or not you want to have any marsupial Fera (in the past or in the present) can be a different issue from the Garou specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Dingoes have been in Oz for 12K years thats easily long enough for them to have a small isolated presence, granted not as long as the approx 80K that humans have been. And as mentioned Wild Dog Men are actually present in a fair number of Dreamings. The 12K actually ties in better time wise with the Singing Dog Garou in Papua ( A World of Rage 20th) as well.<br /> <br /> I don't think theres any need to make them a Tribe but rather something more like the Siberahk but with Talon and Gnawer influences rather than Fang and Younger Brother.<br /> <br /> They would still be some of the least common of the native Fera though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T16:36:32-07:00","id":1448547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448546#post1448546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, Dingoes have been in Oz for 12K years thats easily long enough for them to have a small isolated presence, granted not as long as the approx 80K that humans have been. And as mentioned Wild Dog Men are actually present in a fair number of Dreamings. The 12K actually ties in better time wise with the Singing Dog Garou in Papua ( A World of Rage 20th) as well.<br /> <br /> I don't think theres any need to make them a Tribe but rather something more like the Siberahk but with Talon and Gnawer influences rather than Fang and Younger Brother.<br /> <br /> They would still be some of the least common of the native Fera though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I assume pre-European contact, the Anansi and the Mokole were the dominant Fera in Australia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T16:43:48-07:00","id":1448548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448547#post1448547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah I assume pre-European contact, the Anansi and the Mokole were the dominant Fera in Australia.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ananasi, Camazotz, Nagah, Gumargan, Corax, Rokea ( with grudging acceptance of the ' Dogs' ) should all be present. All of them are important Dreaming Ancestors whose stories reflect fairly well those Fera.<br /> <br /> Australia probably should have had an existing, though far flung, Ahadi/Beast Courts type arrangement that was heavily impacted by colonising Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 05-15-2021, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T17:56:38-07:00","id":1448552,"title":"","content":"I keep trying to imagine were-kangaroos, but the visual image just doesn't work. <br /> <br /> In my own head canon, I've always imagined the pre-European North American breeds as having something akin to the Ahadi, where the Three Brothers and the Three Sisters (the Bastet tribes) saw themselves as meant to be complimentary to each other and balance out their closest neighbor (Balam and Uktena, for example), with the Gurahl, Nuwisha, and Corax (and bats) taking an advisory role, and the Mokole and Ananasi being a step removed from that (and the Nagah being another step or two from that). <br /> <br /> Australia I've never really known enough about the native culture to be comfortable with more than vague generalities, but for them I'd guess something where each group keeps to its own areas, with the Corax (and bats?) carrying messages between them, and then the semi-regular gatherings of diplomatic representatives or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-14T21:14:27-07:00","id":1448567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448552#post1448552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep trying to imagine were-kangaroos, but the visual image just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> In my own head canon, I've always imagined the pre-European North American breeds as having something akin to the Ahadi, where the Three Brothers and the Three Sisters (the Bastet tribes) saw themselves as meant to be complimentary to each other and balance out their closest neighbor (Balam and Uktena, for example), with the Gurahl, Nuwisha, and Corax (and bats) taking an advisory role, and the Mokole and Ananasi being a step removed from that (and the Nagah being another step or two from that).<br /> <br /> Australia I've never really known enough about the native culture to be comfortable with more than vague generalities, but for them I'd guess something where each group keeps to its own areas, with the Corax (and bats?) carrying messages between them, and then the semi-regular gatherings of diplomatic representatives or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> * Edits Camazotz into post. Always forget about them.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T05:49:23-07:00","id":1448580,"title":"","content":"Instead of renaming the indigenous tribe, I would do a more deep genetic study creating new inner factions culturally different, with different ethnicites inside them, but without losing a cultural-genetic connection.<br /> A northern italian Fianna would never be the same of a scottish one.<br /> An ugric Wendigo will never be the same as a northern american one and so on.<br /> So, ''Wendigo'' and ''Uktena'' would be just the tribal totem name, and the name the other tribes use to refer to them, even sometimes in a derogative way (after all, wta's tragedy, is made up by feuds, breeding stock and so on), with the inner factions calling themselves in other ways, but connected by the same totem.<br /> <br /> But this is just how my party like it. We are all speculating on this kind of things about w5. <br /> Reading a lot of nice ideas here guys. Keep writing!<br /> Salute","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T07:04:54-07:00","id":1448583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448540#post1448540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The history of the setting makes this... not as bad as it could be. The real big outliers are the White Howlers.<br /> <br /> The Fianna's pre-Phoenician expansion territory included modern day: Portugal, Spain, France, and the UK, with the Get of Fenris controlling Norway, Sweden, Finland, Denmark, Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania, and Poland. That's not exactly small parts of Europe. With the Black Furies making up most of southern Europe, and the Shadow Lords expanding into the area from the Caucus range.<br /> <br /> So the White Howlers only being from a part of the UK? That's definitely the oddball.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs both traditionally claimed territories on the Europe/Asia border. The Silver Fangs have three Houses that are mostly Asian (Crescent Moon over northern Asia, Wise Heart over western Asia, and Blood Red Crest over the Indian sub-continent). The Children of Gaia explicitly started in the Fertile Crescent, while the Shadow Lords and Glass Walkers have later, but significant numbers in the Middle Kingdom (the fact that the Middle Kingdom is its own separate thing is a huge portion of the problem here). And of course the Stargazers.<br /> <br /> South America also runs into the problem that sub-Saharan Africa does: a lack of significant populations of wolves to drawn on for cultural inspirations for Tribes from there, and the game being weird about canids that count or don't for these things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, you can fix a lot by expanding the Stargazers so they're not a tiny group of Buddhist monks that refuse to reproduce with the large wolf and human populations around them. As I've gone on about in other threads, the Stargazers could easily be one of the largest Tribes, and add a lot more to Asian representation in the Garou nation; esp, if you have an Asian/Oceania Tribe made of expanding out the singing dogs/dingoes into something more.<br /> <br /> Though we're getting away from brain-storming names for the American Tribes.<br /> <br /> I'm still curious if other people have thoughts about my idea of using more neutral names, but ones that still denote a difference in culture. While it might have been facetious, if the American Tribes had names in the format like Hunters in Darkness, instead of Shadow Lords is an example of a way you can do something to address what I did before.</div> </div> </div> </div>They happened to have a Garou tribe in Australia of all places so k can totally see were manned wolfs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T13:44:49-07:00","id":1448616,"title":"","content":"I've long advocated for expanding the number of canids that the Garou can mate with successfully. Esp. since it means we don't need Mokole handwave ritual magic to justify having some non-wolf Garou.<br /> <br /> That said, as this thread has pointed out, the Bunyip thing is its own mess of problems to try to clean up; so probably isn't the best thing to lean on in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T14:20:12-07:00","id":1448625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448616#post1448616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, as this thread has pointed out, the Bunyip thing is its own mess of problems to try to clean up; so probably isn't the best thing to lean on in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Widening the list of Canid options is fine, Bunyip needing the assistance by merit of not being Canids would probably be just fine, it would keep the Were-Marsupials sufficiently Unique.<br /> <br /> what statistic differences would the other Canids Confer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T15:43:06-07:00","id":1448629,"title":"","content":"I realize, as I was typing stuff, I was making a bit of an assumption.<br /> <br /> Do you mean statistic differences such as form stats, or demographics, or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T18:27:07-07:00","id":1448644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448616#post1448616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've long advocated for expanding the number of canids that the Garou can mate with successfully. Esp. since it means we don't need Mokole handwave ritual magic to justify having some non-wolf Garou.<br /> <br /> That said, as this thread has pointed out, the Bunyip thing is its own mess of problems to try to clean up; so probably isn't the best thing to lean on in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not actually a handwave; there's a procedure for it, albeit under a Shining Auspice Rank 5 Gift. There's also a rite that duplicates their suspended animation long sleep Gift, so it probably follows a similar pattern - duplicating the effects of the Gift, but on someone else's behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T09:03:16-07:00","id":1448871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448521#post1448521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally use Older Brother, Middle Brother, and Younger Brother but I can understand why those wouldn\u2019t be particularly attractive as primary names.<br /> <br /> For Older Brother I\u2019ve heard of \u2018Bane Tenders\u2019 and I can also imagine names like \u2018Dark Whisperers\u2019, \u2018Shadow Wresters\u2019, or \u2018Serpent Handlers\u2019. I can also see \u2018Whisper Keepers\u2019 and I also tend to handle their tribal patron as \u201cHorned Serpent\u201d with a focus on the dangerous but rewarding task of delving underground or into dark/secret places to discover hidden/powerful knowledge.<br /> <br /> For Middle Brother I\u2019ve heard \u2018Land Keepers\u2019 or \u2018Earth Walkers\u2019, \u2018World Speakers\u2019, or \u2018Law Tellers\u2019. For their tribal patron I usually keep it as something like Turtle or \u201cLand Turtle\u201d with an emphasis on the steady and enduring laws and orders of the world kept by tradition and communion with your environment, history, and society.<br /> <br /> For Younger Brother I\u2019ve heard \u2018Ice Hearts\u2019 and I can imagine options like \u2018Ice Hunters\u2019, \u2018Wind Biters\u2019, and I can certainly see \u2018Winter Claws\u2019. For their tribal patron I usually use something like \u201cForest Man/Hairy Man\u201d, somewhat inspired by the already apparent use of Sasquatch but also references I\u2019ve found in other indigenous American cultures in my research and seemed to have both a primeval wilderness and custom keeper elements. I can also see how Great Fisher would work well though.<br /> <br /> For the Australian \u201cGarou\u201d I usually have them be a unique fera native to Australia that was post-humously inducted into the nation by guilty and grieving garou. I usually call them something like the \u2018Song Keepers\u2019 and place a focus on their being keepers of rituals and oral histories, now lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to keep the Three Brothers as the official names, with the names given in the published materials used either as pejoratives or by Garou ignorant of the reason those names are used. As a real world corollary, Sioux is not the traditional name for the Dakota, Nakota, and Lakota peoples. It was shortened from the term used for them by an antagonistic tribe, the Ojibwe people, and means &quot;little snakes&quot; or enemy. Most people in the USA still refer to these peoples as the Sioux and do not realize why they should not do so. Despite Garou populations being much smaller, the native tribes still put up with the same $#!^ as their kinfolk every day...<br /> <br /> Your alternate suggestions are good, and better than anything I came up with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T09:06:48-07:00","id":1448873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448552#post1448552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep trying to imagine were-kangaroos, but the visual image just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> In my own head canon, I've always imagined the pre-European North American breeds as having something akin to the Ahadi, where the Three Brothers and the Three Sisters (the Bastet tribes) saw themselves as meant to be complimentary to each other and balance out their closest neighbor (Balam and Uktena, for example), with the Gurahl, Nuwisha, and Corax (and bats) taking an advisory role, and the Mokole and Ananasi being a step removed from that (and the Nagah being another step or two from that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wanted to run a pre-contact North American Fera game, and this has generally been my take on the situation. Using the Bastet as the Three Sisters is intriguing and I thank you for the idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T03:57:45-07:00","id":1448959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1448437-renaming-the-indigenous-tribes?p=1448871#post1448871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to keep the Three Brothers as the official names, with the names given in the published materials used either as pejoratives or by Garou ignorant of the reason those names are used. As a real world corollary, Sioux is not the traditional name for the Dakota, Nakota, and Lakota peoples. It was shortened from the term used for them by an antagonistic tribe, the Ojibwe people, and means &amp;quot;little snakes&amp;quot; or enemy. Most people in the USA still refer to these peoples as the Sioux and do not realize why they should not do so. Despite Garou populations being much smaller, the native tribes still put up with the same $#!^ as their kinfolk every day...<br /> <br /> Your alternate suggestions are good, and better than anything I came up with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s my head cannon to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}